I'd really really like to not mix AbortSignal and some other abort mechanism. But I agree with both: returning an object is really nice DX, and leveraging AbortSignal is really intuitive for people who know the API.

What about this?

```ts
/* Example 1: default signal control */
const response = session.prompt("Do some work");
// ... do some stuff
response.signal.abort("escape");

/* Example 2: timeout */
const {text} = await session.prompt("Do some work", {
