```

Basically, we create a default AbortSignal if you don't provide one, and then you use that. 

I think the thing about https://github.com/electric-sql/electric/issues/4278 is that it's really for sending a signal to the entire agent, like a `running` agent and an `stopping` agent handle `SIGTERM` differently. But when you're on a prompt-by-prompt level like we're talking about here, that doesn't really make sense. At the prompt level, all you have is "I am aborting this in-progress prompt". Or maybe you have pause/resume as well, but that doesn't seem worth inventing an entire clever different system.

I think the `SIG*` system (or something like it) would make more sense at the agent level and URL level, for like an admin API and *stopping long-running agents*, not just prompts. But I think we're pretty far awwy from solving that, and would need better lifecycle control over the agent first, which we don't have.

